Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: channel: use the 19.2 MHz IRIS configuration

The wcn3660b compatible selects use_48mhz_xo=true in qcom_wcnss_iris.c.
On the tested Moto G7 Play this leaves WCNSS waiting for the ready
interrupt until qcom-wcnss-pil reports start timed out (-110).

Use the wcn3620 configuration, which selects 19.2 MHz with the same
regulator voltage requirements. With this change WCNSS reaches running,
wlan0 scans and associates, and IP traffic succeeds over Wi-Fi.

Base: channel-linux f28fca88764982aeef2a251b618686c31f2475d8.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-motorola-channel.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-motorola-channel.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-motorola-channel.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-motorola-channel.dts
@@ -402,10 +402,10 @@
 &wcnss_iris {
 	/*
-	 * Stock shows a Pronto-v3 WCNSS; the G7 family pairs SDM632 with
-	 * the WCN3660B (b/g/n, same as river). Confirm the FW version
-	 * string on hardware.
+	 * Channel requires the 19.2 MHz IRIS XO configuration. The 48 MHz
+	 * configuration selected by wcn3660b causes WCNSS startup to time
+	 * out before the Wi-Fi interface can be registered.
 	 */
-	compatible = "qcom,wcn3660b";
+	compatible = "qcom,wcn3620";
 	vddxo-supply = <&pm8953_l7>;
 	vddrfa-supply = <&pm8953_l19>;
 	vddpa-supply = <&pm8953_l9>;
